11|0@UFOs^1440437376#cue39ax:CaerBannog$:There is zero evidence of ETs visiting Earth. By evidence I mean testable, verifiable evidence. This is the unspoken heresy of UFO research. There is not a molecule of solid evidence to support the idea that ET visits our planet, despite 60+ years of adorable enthusiasts asserting boldly that it is the case. Crash retrievals are even more questionable, obviously. It may surprise you to learn that the elemental origins of the crash retrieval story dates back to at least 1878, and maybe earlier. This fact undermines the claim that such events are historical reality and suggests more that they are folkloric. You appear to have entered into this with a belief system already set up. You appear possessed with the conviction that you know what is really going on. This is common among UFO fans, and it is one of the major reasons why we are no closer to understanding the UFO enigma than we were 40 years ago. Why? Because this kind of attitude is ludicrous to anyone who is not a believer, the very people needed to take this subject out of the fringe, and because it prevents any real discovery of what is actually occurring. It is based on the fantasy of what one wishes to be true, rather than what actually is. Nobody can learn anything new with this viewpoint. It becomes like religious faith. It is ironic that you point to Jacques Vallée, who happens to be one of the great iconoclasts of UFOlogy, who has said as much as I have done at much greater length. He advocates the abandonment of UFO folklore and castigated the true believers' mindset as a dangerous. Neither you nor, I suspect, any human alive really knows what is going on with this phenomenon. People have literally been saying the exact same things you have posted since the 1950 publication of Donald Keyhoe's "The Flying Saucers Are Real". It is this risible certitude in the face of an absolute dearth of verifiable evidence that has made UFO research a laughingstock for decades. My view is to walk back from the absolutism of belief and wipe the slate clean, reassess everything completely objectively, and ditch all presuppositions. That is the only way to change anything. Nothing will happen until we do. 
