5|0@UFOs^1440471942#cueoomw:CaerBannog$:&gt;this is overstatement. Even for you. If there were verified evidence of ET visiting Earth, this sub wouldn't exist. Now, the other points you raise are speculative. Whether there is evidence held in secret somewhere is irrelevant, we don't have it. And arguing the semantics of verifiable verses verified is missing the point: we don't have this evidence. I agree there is a lot of circumstantial evidence, but it doesn't definitively suggest ETH, as we know. &gt; Betty Hill's "star map" Is incorrect. Zeta Reticulum is too young and, we now know, in a different configuration than the map. In any case, the map is not evidence on its own. It is not scientific evidence. 
