0|0@UFOs^1440464322#cuek5ft:Crimfants$:OK, I will try to answer this patiently. Just once. The old saw (decades old) about UFO eyewitness testimony being reliable because it is used as evidence in court cases is fallacious because of the hidden assumption that legal standards of evidence are the same as scientific standards. That is false on its face. Furthermore, there has been a lot of [research into eyewitness testimony, wrongful convictions, and false memories](http://news.sciencemag.org/policy/2014/10/how-reliable-eyewitness-testimony-scientists-weigh) - and the news isn't good. People can and often do, with no malicious intent or mental illness, remember things that never happened, or remember many details completely wrong, and police and prosecutors know how to encourage the bias they want. A police lineup, for example, can actually pressure people to invent memories. I feel strongly that no one should be convicted of any crime on the basis of a single eyewitness. But even so, legal standards *are the wrong standard*. We know that bias and error can creep into scientific work as well. We can never just relax and accept any result without serious scrutiny. Faith has no place in science. As to your second point, there was no point, just a personal attack. I have [already explained](http://apicasefiles.libsyn.com) in plenty of detail what I am about in Unidentified Science, and what my agenda is, and I walk the talk. I'm out there investigating good cases and looking for the right evidence and dealing with the inevitable frustration. 
